      "text": "We will first simplify each fraction individually using the technique of rationalizing the denominator.\n\nFor the first fraction, the conjugate of the denominator is \\(3 + 5i\\). So we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(3 + 5i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} = \\frac{9 + 30i + 25i^2}{9 - 25i^2}.\n\\]\n\nRecall that \\(i^2 = -1\\), so the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{9 + 30i + 25(-1)}{9 - 25(-1)} = \\frac{9 + 30i - 25}{9 + 25} = \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15}{17}i.\n\\]\n\nFor the second fraction, the conjugate of the denominator is \\(3 - 5i\\). So we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(3 - 5i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)} = \\frac{9 - 30i + 25i^2}{9 - 25i^2}.\n\\]\n\nAgain, using \\(i^2 = -1\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{9 - 30i + 25(-1)}{9 - 25(-1)} = \\frac{9 - 30i - 25}{9 + 25} = \\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15}{17}i.\n\\]\n\nNow we can add the simplified fractions:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15}{17}i + -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15}{17}i = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} + \\left(\\frac{15}{17}i - \\frac{15}{17}i\\right) = -\\frac{16}{17} + 0i = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}\\).",
