      "text": "\\[\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\]. To solve the given expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we will proceed step-by-step.\n\nFirst, we simplify each fraction separately by multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator.\n\nFor the first fraction \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\), the conjugate of the denominator is \\(3 + 5i\\). So, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(3 + 5i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the denominator:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nNow, we compute the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)^2 = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i\n\\]\n\nSo, the first fraction simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\nNext, for the second fraction \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), the conjugate of the denominator is \\(3 - 5i\\). So, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(3 - 5i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}\n\\]\n\nWe already know the denominator is 34 from the first fraction. Now, we compute the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)^2 = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i\n\\]\n\nSo, the second fraction simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the two simplified fractions:\n\n\\[\n\\left( -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) + \\left( -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17} + 0i = -\\frac{16}{17}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}\n\\]",
